  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「オヒシバ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%83%92%E3%82%B7%E3%83%90",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106352354,
      "text": "オヒシバ は、イネ科オヒシバ属の植物である。日なたに生える、それほど背の高くない一年生草本で、道端でもよく見かける雑草である。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Eleusine indica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusine_indica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1212487328,
      "text": "Eleusine indica, the Indian goosegrass, yard-grass, goosegrass, wiregrass, or crowfootgrass, is a species of grass in the family Poaceae. It is a small annual grass distributed throughout the warmer areas of the world to about 50 degrees latitude. It is an invasive species in some areas."
    }
  },
